cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use banjir3d or its results, please cite it as below, name the run (provenance JSON of the export) and cite the datasets listed on the Data page."
title: "banjir3d: browser flood simulation for Jakarta (local inertial 2D model with open data)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "banjir3d project"
repository-code: "https://github.com/raredil/banjir3d"
url: "https://raredil.github.io/banjir3d/"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
version: "2026-11-20"
abstract: >-
  Web application that simulates pluvial and river flooding over DKI Jakarta and 10 km around it with a local inertial
  shallow-water model (WebGPU with a CPU fallback), curve-number infiltration, upstream inflows, land subsidence and mapped
  drains, from open data. Scores against three observed floods, methods, references and every assumption are on the
  Methods and Validation pages. Not a forecast of which street or RW floods.
keywords:
  - flood
  - hydrodynamic model
  - Jakarta
  - WebGPU
  - open data
